Signed-off-by: Aayush Nair <aayushnair204@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 init/Kconfig                            |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst
index 91beaa6798ce02817546fdde8dfa6659bc9415ab..09a9b116d4dce6a3f35c959ae7ddbc88cada570b 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst
@@ -78,6 +78,7 @@ v1 is available under :ref:`Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v1/index.rst <cgrou
        5.10-2 Migration and Ownership
      5-11. Others
        5-11-1. perf_event
+       5-11-2. kairos
      5-N. Non-normative information
        5-N-1. CPU controller root cgroup process behaviour
        5-N-2. IO controller root cgroup process behaviour
@@ -2957,6 +2958,35 @@ automatically enabled on the v2 hierarchy so that perf events can
 always be filtered by cgroup v2 path.  The controller can still be
 moved to a legacy hierarchy after v2 hierarchy is populated.
 
+kairos
+~~~~~~
+
+The kairos controller gives every cgroup a task class: latency-critical
+("lc") or batch, so that the parts of the kernel which schedule tasks
+and share resources between them can tell a latency-critical service
+from the batch work running next to it.  Like perf_event, it is enabled
+on every cgroup of the v2 hierarchy without being listed in
+"cgroup.subtree_control".  It is enabled by the CONFIG_CGROUP_KAIROS
+config option.
+
+A cgroup takes its parent's class unless it has a class of its own.
+The root cgroup is always "lc".
+
+  kairos.class
+	A read-write single value file which exists on non-root
+	cgroups.  The default is "inherit".
+
+	"lc" or "batch" gives the cgroup a class of its own; "inherit"
+	makes it take its parent's.
+
+  kairos.class.effective
+	A read-only single value file which exists on non-root cgroups.
+
+	The class in effect: "lc" or "batch".  A write to a cgroup's
+	"kairos.class" changes this in the cgroup and in every cgroup
+	below it which inherits, down to the first one with a class of
+	its own.
+
 
 Non-normative information
 -------------------------
diff --git a/init/Kconfig b/init/Kconfig
index 971c3bca12ed634a67b856290123deb374d3e227..069747430e13efb9e090079890ed2c6336d9ca88 100644
--- a/init/Kconfig
+++ b/init/Kconfig
@@ -1358,6 +1358,9 @@ config CGROUP_KAIROS
 
 	  Kairos's BPF scheduler tells the two classes apart by it.
 
+	  For more information, see the kairos section in
+	  Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst.
+
 config CGROUP_DEBUG
 	bool "Debug controller"
 	default n
